  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If all the points of a scatter diagram lie on a straight line rising from left to right, the correlation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "low positive"
   },
   {
    "en": "perfect positive (r = +1)"
   },
   {
    "en": "zero"
   },
   {
    "en": "perfect negative (r = −1)"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "Points exactly on a rising line mean perfect positive correlation."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q04",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t1",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If r = 0 between two variables, it means that:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "one is twice the other"
   },
   {
    "en": "they are independent in every way"
   },
   {
    "en": "they are perfectly related"
   },
   {
    "en": "there is no linear relationship between them"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 3,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "r = 0 means the variables are uncorrelated (no linear relationship). They may still have a non-linear relation."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q05",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "The coefficient of correlation r always lies between:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0 and ∞"
   },
   {
    "en": "−1 and +1"
   },
   {
    "en": "−∞ and +∞"
   },
   {
    "en": "0 and 1"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "By its definition (Cauchy–Schwarz inequality), −1 ≤ r ≤ 1."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q06",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If Cov(x, y) = 3, σₓ = 2 and σᵧ = 2, then r is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.375"
   },
   {
    "en": "3"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.75"
   },
   {
    "en": "1.5"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "r = Cov(x, y)/(σₓσᵧ) = 3/4 = 0.75."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q07",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If Cov(x, y) = 12, Var(x) = 16 and Var(y) = 25, then r is:"
