   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q08",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t2",
  "stem": {
   "en": "If r(x, y) = 0.6, u = (x − 10)/2 and v = (y − 5)/(−3), then r(u, v) is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.6"
   },
   {
    "en": "−0.6"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.4"
   },
   {
    "en": "−0.4"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "r is unaffected by change of origin and of scale, except that the sign flips when the two scale factors have opposite signs. Here 2 and −3 have opposite signs, so r(u, v) = −0.6."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "tags": [],
  "solution": [
   {
    "en": "r is unaffected by change of origin and of scale, except that the sign flips when the two scale factors have opposite signs."
   },
   {
    "en": "Here 2 and −3 have opposite signs, so r(u, v) = −0.6."
   }
  ]
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q09",
  "chapterId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression",
  "topicId": "puc1-statistics-08-correlation-and-regression.t3",
  "stem": {
   "en": "For n = 5 pairs of ranks, ΣD² = 10. Spearman's rank correlation is:"
  },
  "options": [
   {
    "en": "0.25"
   },
   {
    "en": "−0.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.5"
   },
   {
    "en": "0.9"
   }
  ],
  "answer": 2,
  "explanation": {
   "en": "ρ = 1 − 6ΣD²/[n(n² − 1)] = 1 − 60/120 = 0.5."
  },
  "exams": [
   "PUC"
  ],
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "tags": []
 },
 {
  "id": "1t08-q10",
